VeridianOS: users KCM: no fprintd properties qdbusxml2cpp cannot name

qdbusxml2cpp warned four times (kcms/users/src/net.reactivated.Fprint.
Device.xml): "Invalid D-Bus member name 'num-enroll-stages' found in
interface 'net.reactivated.Fprint.Device'" (and scan-type,
finger-present, finger-needed). fprintd names these properties with
dashes, which D-Bus member names cannot contain, so the generated proxy
never had accessors for them: qdbusxml2cpp skips them. The KCM reads them
by name through org.freedesktop.DBus.Properties.Get (fprintdevice.cpp).
The four elements are removed from the interface description used for
the proxy, which is generated exactly as before; the property names are
recorded in a comment there.

